    "turn_text": "we announced our plans yesterday. There will be a promenade right through the middle of George Brown. It will establish retail. There'll be ultimately another convention hotel. So we will have a convention destination that people around the state and the nation want to come to. But even more importantly, I think it'll be a venue that Houstonians want to go down and visit. It'll be quite an entertainment. People leave the ball parts. They don't want to go home after winning a World Series game. So they'll walk down. to the George R Brown Entertainment District and it will really, really improve central Houston. All great cities have to have a viable downtown. It'll open up the east side. 45 and 59 by the state are being placed underground. There'll be a 30 acre footprint there, a green space. So you open up the east side, it'll open up to the animal area. And so it'll be a win-win for the city of a generate revenue. We'll plow that back into city services. All right, sir. Mr. Mayor got a run, but I want to thank you for your time as always, sir. Appreciate it. That is Houston Mayor John Whitmire. OK, there you go. The improvements coming to the Georgia are brown. $2 billion worth. And I get investing in the convention center, I do. If you want to track conventions, then you've got to have the right conventions that are in order to do that. So we've got a lot of things going in our favor, but that's something you just really have to keep up with. All right, can I complain about something? First of all, I'm on vacation next week. I should mention that, right? We'll be doing some best stuffs next week on the show, some best of interviews and what have you. Hopefully some stuff that you will enjoy listening to yet again. But",
